  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Financial Analytics & Reporting for a refining company with Processing, Supply Chain, Support, and Corporate divisions across Gulf Coast, Midwest, and National regions. Stakeholders include the CFO (operating margin, ROIC, EBITDA, plan variance), Controllers (cost-center P&L close), and Division VPs (budget variance, OPEX vs. plan).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Operating margin = operating_margin_pct on financial_kpi_monthly; refining industry through-cycle median ~8-10%, top-quartile >15%\n- ROIC = roic_pct; refining top-quartile target >12%, integrated majors 10-15% in mid-cycle\n- EBITDA = ebitda_usd on budget_snapshots; primary capital-allocation lens\n- Plan variance = actual_revenue_usd - planned_revenue_usd (and same for OPEX); >5% adverse triggers commentary\n- Cost per unit = cost_per_unit on financial_kpi_monthly; refining OPEX ex-energy target $3-$5/bbl\n- Account types: Revenue, OPEX, CAPEX, Depreciation, G&A — drives the bridge from gross profit to net income\n- Headcount = headcount on financial_kpi_monthly; revenue / FTE benchmark varies by region and division\n- GL categories (Operations, Maintenance, Labor, Materials, Utilities, Admin) — used for cost driver analysis\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - financial_transactions_metrics (source: financial_transactions) — dims: transaction_date, cost_center_id, division, region, account_type, gl_category; measures: total_amount_usd, total_budget_usd, total_transactions, avg_transaction_usd, max_amount.\n  - budget_snapshots_metrics (source: budget_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_month, cost_center_id, division, region; measures: total_actual_revenue, total_planned_revenue, total_actual_opex, total_ebitda, total_planned_opex, max_planned_revenue.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. cost_center_name, operating_margin_pct, roic_pct, cost_per_unit, headcount).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Top 10 cost centers by total actual revenue over the last 12 months.",
    "Show monthly trend of total EBITDA across the company for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which divisions are running OPEX over plan year-to-date, and by how much?",
    "Top 10 cost centers by adverse revenue variance vs. plan this quarter.",
    "How has operating margin trended month-over-month by division?",
    "Which regions have the highest ROIC, ranked best to worst?",
    "What is the OPEX-to-revenue ratio by division this quarter?"
